{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"comic-heavyset-jerboa","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nOn Windows, `git show <rev>:<path>` run without `--` dies with exit 128 and `fatal: failed to stat '<rev>:<path>': Filename too long` when the working directory plus the argument exceeds MAX_PATH. Git stats each revision argument as a possible filename to rule out ambiguity, and it aborts on any stat error other than ENOENT. Measured in Windows `sweep (windows)` diagnostic run 44899637411 (2026-11-21 PST): `fsck_restore`'s `git show <sha>^:<ticket>/<event>.json` failed this way under a pytest temp dir. The same test passed under a shorter temp path (run 44899366277). With `git cat-file blob` (which takes only an object name) it passed (run 44900309390). cold-censorable-armedcrab fixes the `fsck_restore` sites. This ticket covers the rest.\n\n## Sites on origin/main 1a11014a3a4 that read `<rev>:<path>` through `git show` with no `--`\n- src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py:98, :122, :164 (`tickets:.gitattributes`, `tickets:.gitignore`, `tickets:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/init.py:440 (`tickets:.pre-commit-config.yaml`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py:108 (`<rev>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:151 (`<tickets ref>:<path>`)\n- src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:107 (`<spec>`)\n- src/rebar/_store/compat.py:180, :274 (`<remote ref>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py:67 (`tickets:<projects.json>`)\n- src/rebar/_store/reclaim_eligibility.py:101\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:217 (`HEAD:<path>`)\n\nSeveral of these treat a non-zero exit as \"absent\", so a deep Windows path would misread an existing object as missing. One example is the `_init_ensures` units, which would then re-create and commit a file that exists.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven per site)\nEvery site above can hit this on a deep enough Windows path. Short ref:path pairs under a shallow tracker path stay under MAX_PATH and never do.\n\n## Proposed direction\nRoute these reads through `git cat-file blob <rev>:<path>`, or add `--` after the revision, and add a regression test that drives each read with a cwd deep enough to exceed MAX_PATH on Windows.","id":"8c3d-a931-4c0b-4792","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"git show <rev>:<path> dies with 'Filename too long' on deep Windows paths"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795261581107500001,"uuid":"9401ab2e-cf7a-4ac2-8c97-3f393e65220d"}